meta {
  name: Screen - Postprocess (re-run)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/me/screen/{{session_id}}/postprocess
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

params:query {
  ~force: true
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.session_id: isDefined
  res.body.history_id: isDefined
  res.body.status: isDefined
  res.body.metadata: isDefined
  res.body.metadata.ahrq_status: isDefined
}

docs {
  Re-trigger the ARHQ post-processing callback for an existing screening session.
  Keyed only by `session_id` — an idempotent, id-triggered reprocess. Same logic
  as the automatic run at end of `/reply`: a second LLM call extracts scores +
  comments into strict JSON, the result is written to `feature_history.metadata`
  on the latest history row AND returned here.

  Query params:
    - `force=true` — allow re-run even if the session hasn't covered all 23
      questions yet (admin / QA). Default false → 409 on incomplete sessions.

  Use cases:
    - Retry after a prior failed run (poll `/postprocess/status` first — zero
      LLM cost — then re-POST here). Never 500s on extractor errors, so a client
      can safely loop retry-on-failure.
    - Re-score after tweaking the rubric / severity thresholds in
      `app/policies/ahrq.py`.
    - Backfill sessions that completed before the callback existed
      (status `not_started`).

  Response shape (PostProcessRunDTO):
    {
      "session_id": "...",
      "history_id": "...",
      "status": "success" | "failed",
      "metadata": {
        "ahrq_status": "success" | "failed",
        "ahrq_started_at": "2026-07-03T12:34:56Z",
        "ahrq_finished_at": "2026-07-03T12:35:12Z",
        "ahrq_scores": [2, 3, 1, ...] | null,     // 15 ints, chosen column 0-4 (0 = unanswered)
        "ahrq_comments": "slow reader;heavy,..." | null,  // comma-sep, index-aligned
        "ahrq_total": 45 | null,                  // weighted, range 22-88
        "ahrq_max_total": 88,
        "ahrq_severity": "unlikely" | "mild" | "moderate_severe" | null, // <45 | 45-60 | >60
        "ahrq_disclaimer": "...",                 // always display
        "ahrq_attribution": "© Ian Smythe & John Everatt, 2001.",
        "ahrq_error": null | { "reason": "...", "message": "..." }
      }
    }

  Note: commas inside an individual comment are sanitized to ';' so the
  comma-join stays index-aligned — they are NOT a failure.

  Status codes:
    200 — post-processing completed (status may still be "failed" — errors don't 500 here)
    403 — session belongs to another user
    404 — session or history row missing
    409 — session not complete yet AND force=false
}
